  "content": {
    "id": "p70-q23-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "Factorise $x^4-x^3-5x^2+12$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x-2)^2(x^2+3x+3)$.",
      "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^4-x^3-5x^2+12$. Test an integer factor of $12$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(2)&=16-8-20+12\\\\&=0.\\end{aligned}$$\nSo $x-2$ is a factor. Polynomial long division gives\n$$\\begin{array}{r|rrrr} &x^3&+x^2&-3x&-6\\\\\\hline x-2&x^4&-x^3&-5x^2&+0x+12\\\\ &x^4&-2x^3&&\\\\\\hline &&x^3&-5x^2&+0x+12\\\\ &&x^3&-2x^2&\\\\\\hline &&&-3x^2&+0x+12\\\\ &&&-3x^2&+6x\\\\\\hline &&&&-6x+12\\\\ &&&&-6x+12\\\\\\hline &&&&0\\end{array}$$\nFor $Q(x)=x^3+x^2-3x-6$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}Q(2)&=8+4-6-6\\\\&=0.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $x-2$ is also a factor of $Q(x)$. Dividing again:\n$$\\begin{array}{r|rrr} &x^2&+3x&+3\\\\\\hline x-2&x^3&+x^2&-3x-6\\\\ &x^3&-2x^2&\\\\\\hline &&3x^2&-3x-6\\\\ &&3x^2&-6x\\\\\\hline &&&3x-6\\\\ &&&3x-6\\\\\\hline &&&0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(x)&=(x-2)(x^3+x^2-3x-6)\\\\&=(x-2)^2(x^2+3x+3).\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
